WEBVTT

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:02.829
The fictional inventory is ready, but the actual

00:00:03.054 --> 00:00:06.826
business-account approval is unknown. Do not infer permission

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:09.746
from an AI answer. Record who can authorize

00:00:09.881 --> 00:00:13.374
use and which organizational policy applies. Check the

00:00:13.419 --> 00:00:18.674
actual account, device, access, sharing, retention and vendor

00:00:18.719 --> 00:00:22.401
terms against current official sources. If suitability remains

00:00:22.536 --> 00:00:26.084
unconfirmed, pause real use and continue with fictional

00:00:26.219 --> 00:00:29.920
substitutes. Plan the exit: keep sanitized evidence in

00:00:29.964 --> 00:00:32.839
its authorized location and follow the permitted handling

00:00:32.928 --> 00:00:36.387
process for temporary copies. A visible deletion alone

00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:39.297
does not prove every provider copy is removed.

00:00:39.602 --> 00:00:42.701
This example demonstrates a responsible pause, not a

00:00:42.746 --> 00:00:44.593
verified real-world approval.
